<title>UK: Salehurst jumps to premium on market debut.</title>
<headline>Salehurst jumps to premium on market debut.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in specialist paper distributor Salehurst Plc climbed to a premium on Tuesday on their first day of dealings on the London Stock Exchange.</p>
<p>The company's shares, issued at 117p, gained 7p to 124p by 1105 GMT in what dealers described as thin volume.</p>
<p>Salehurst, valued at around 15.5 million stg at the issue price, raised about two million stg of new money in the flotation and said it would use the proceeds to cut debt and take advantage of growth opportunities.</p>
<p>The company, which purchases and supplies paper primarily to magazine publishers, said it would consider an acquisition but had no specific target in mind.</p>
<p>-- Andrew Langlands, London newsroom +44 171 542 3496</p>
